# Environment / secrets
.env

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
*.log
# …except the test corpus. Every MongoDB Log Summary fixture is a mongod log and mongod
# names its log `.log`, so the blanket rule above silently kept all eight scenarios out of
# the repo — the tests passed locally and would have failed on a fresh clone. The Galera and
# Group Replication fixtures escaped only because MySQL calls its error log `.err`.
!app/testdata/**/*.log

# The PXC operator's own deploy/cr.yaml, fetched into the test corpus so the three cr.yaml
# transform tests can run (IMPLEMENTATION.md §366 has the one-line curl). It is a verbatim copy of
# an upstream file rather than a fixture of ours, so it stays out of the repo — and ignoring it by
# name keeps `git add -A` from sweeping it back in.
#
# By NAME, deliberately, not as `app/testdata/`: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a directory rule here would silently defeat the negation above and make the whole log corpus
# uncommittable again — the exact bug that line was added to fix.
app/testdata/cr.yaml
# The same for the operator's CustomResourceDefinition, captured from a running cluster with
# `kubectl get crd perconaxtradbclusters.pxc.percona.com -o json` (IMPLEMENTATION.md). The custom
# resource editor's tests build their form from it, because the thing worth testing about a
# schema pruner is what it does to the real 1.4 MB schema — a hand-written fixture would only
# prove the pruner works on fixtures.
app/testdata/pxc-crd.json

# Screenshot-capture tooling — maintainer-only, kept out of the repo.
# The generated screenshots (docs/screenshots/*.png) ARE committed; only the
# machinery that produces them is ignored.
/app/web/scripts/

# Cross-compiled dbcanvas-cli binaries (`make cli`)
/dist/

# Go
/app/*.db
/app/*.db-*
/app/dbcanvas
# `go build ./...` in cli/ drops the binary next to its source, named after the module.
/cli/dbcanvas-cli

# OS
.DS_Store

# vite SSR bundle for the render smoke test (npm run smoke)
app/web/.smoke/

# images.yaml — what `make images` built on THIS machine, and only this machine: one entry per
# OS x version for the single platform DOCKER_PLATFORM selects. versions.yaml is committed
# because it is a catalogue of what those images can install, which is the same everywhere and
# costs hours to probe; this is a record of a local build, which costs one `make images`.
#
# Nothing breaks by its absence: `make env` drops an `images: []` stand-in so Docker cannot
# create a directory in its place, and loadImageCatalog falls back to the image entries in the
# committed versions.yaml until the next build writes this file.
/images.yaml
